#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:23
msgid "Set locale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Ubuntu-Set-Locale.rst:5
msgid ""
"Make sure you have a locale which supports ``UTF-8``. If you are in a "
"minimal environment (such as a docker container), the locale may be "
"something minimal like ``POSIX``. We test with the following settings. "
"However, it should be fine if you're using a different UTF-8 supported "
"locale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Ubuntu-Set-Locale.rst:10
msgid ""
"$ locale  # check for UTF-8\n"
"\n"
"$ sudo apt update && sudo apt install locales\n"
"$ sudo locale-gen en_US en_US.UTF-8\n"
"$ sudo update-locale LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8 LANG=en_US.UTF-8\n"
"$ export LANG=en_US.UTF-8\n"
"\n"
"$ locale  # verify settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:28
msgid "Create a location for the ROS 2 installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:30
msgid ""
"This location will contain both the installed binary packages, plus the ROS "
"2 installation itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:32
msgid "Start a terminal, then create a directory to store the installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:34
msgid "$ mkdir ~/ros_ws_pixi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:39
msgid "Install prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:42
msgid "Install pixi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:44
msgid ""
"ROS 2 uses `conda-forge <https://conda-forge.org/>`__ as a backend for "
"packages, with `pixi <https://pixi.sh/latest/>`__ as the frontend."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:46
msgid ""
"Continue using the previous terminal session, and use the instructions from "
"https://pixi.sh/latest/ to install ``pixi``. Once ``pixi`` has been "
"installed, close the terminal session and start it again, which will ensure "
"``pixi`` is on the PATH."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:50
msgid "Install dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:52
msgid "Download the pixi configuration file in the existing terminal session:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:54
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros_ws_pixi\n"
"$ wget https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ros2/ros2/rolling/pixi.toml -O pixi."
"toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:59
msgid "Install dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:61
msgid "$ pixi install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:66
msgid "Build ROS 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:69
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:116
msgid "Source the pixi environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:71
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:118
msgid ""
"This is required in every command prompt you open to set up paths to the "
"dependencies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:73
#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:120
msgid ""
"$ cd ~/ros_ws_pixi\n"
"$ pixi shell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:79
msgid "Get ROS 2 code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:81
msgid ""
"Now that we have the development tools we can get the ROS 2 source code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:83
msgid "Setup a development folder, for example ``~/ros_ws_pixi/src``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:86
msgid ""
"$ mkdir ~/ros_ws_pixi/src\n"
"$ cd ~/ros_ws_pixi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:91
msgid ""
"Get the ``ros2.repos`` file which defines the repositories to clone from:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:93
msgid ""
"$ vcs import --input https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ros2/ros2/rolling/"
"ros2.repos src"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:98
msgid "Build the code in the workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:100
msgid "To build the workspace folder tree:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:102
msgid ""
"$ colcon build --merge-install --event-handlers console_direct+ --cmake-args "
"-D LTTNGPY_DISABLED=1 --packages-skip qt_gui_cpp --packages-skip-by-dep "
"qt_gui_cpp --packages-skip-build-finished"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:108
msgid ""
"Source installation can take a long time given the large number of packages "
"being pulled into the workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:111
msgid "Setup environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:113
msgid "Start a new terminal, which will be used in the examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:126
msgid "Source the ROS 2 environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:128
msgid ""
"This is required in every command prompt you open to setup the ROS 2 "
"workspace:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:130
msgid "$ source ~/ros_ws_pixi/install/local_setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:134
msgid ""
"This will automatically set up the environment for any DDS vendors for which "
"support was built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:137
msgid "Try some examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:139
msgid "You can run the tests using this command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:141
msgid "$ colcon test --merge-install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:147
msgid ""
"``--merge-install`` should only be used if it was also used in the build "
"step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:149
msgid "Afterwards you can get a summary of the tests using this command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:151
msgid "$ colcon test-result"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:155
msgid ""
"To run the examples, set up the workspace by sourcing the ``local_setup."
"bash`` file. Then, run a C++ ``talker``\\ :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:158
msgid ""
"$ source ~/ros_ws_pixi/install/local_setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:163
msgid ""
"In a separate command prompt you can do the same, but instead run a Python "
"``listener``\\ :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:165
msgid ""
"$ source ~/ros_ws_pixi/install/local_setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_py listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:170
msgid ""
"You should see the ``talker`` saying that it's ``Publishing`` messages and "
"the ``listener`` saying ``I heard`` those messages. This verifies both the C+"
"+ and Python APIs are working properly. Hooray!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:176
msgid ""
"It is not recommended to build in the same cmd prompt that you've sourced "
"the ``local_setup.bash``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:179
msgid "Next steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:181
msgid ""
"Continue with the tutorials to configure your environment, create your own "
"workspace and packages, and learn ROS 2 core concepts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:184
msgid "Stay up to date"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:186
msgid ""
"See :doc:`Maintaining-a-Source-Checkout` to periodically refresh your source "
"installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:188
msgid ""
"If you installed your workspace with colcon as instructed above, "
"\"uninstalling\" could be just a matter of opening a new terminal and not "
"sourcing the workspace's ``setup`` file. This way, your environment will "
"behave as though there is no Rolling install on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:191
msgid ""
"If you're also trying to free up space, you can delete the entire workspace "
"directory with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/Alternatives/Ubuntu-Development-Setup-Pixi.rst:193
msgid "$ rm -rf ~/ros_ws_pixi"
msgstr ""
